{"id": "meta_modelers_guide.composites.fig10-mechanistic", "name": "Biofilm development \u2014 spatially-emergent aggregation, formation, and ECM persistence", "description": "Fig 10 mechanistic variant. Six motile cells on a 2-D box (lattice units) aggregate by LOCAL adhesion toward neighbours; once a quorum sits within form_radius of the centroid for sustain_ticks consecutive ticks the biofilm FORMS \u2014 an emergent place-graph rewrite nesting the cells under a new biofilm node (identity + biomass preserved), after which the collective cohesion port becomes operative. Sessile cells secrete ECM that binds the community; without ECM they spread back apart. Formation is driven by cluster geometry, not a wall clock. Matched-null controls (adhesion off, ECM off \u2014 via epsilon) isolate each arm.", "parameters": {}, "state": {"colony_dynamics": {"_type": "process", "address": "local:BiofilmColony", "interval": 1.0, "config": {"sense_radius": 6.0, "adhesion": 0.35, "repulsion": 0.45, "rep_radius": 1.2, "form_radius": 2.2, "quorum": 4.0, "sustain_ticks": 3.0, "ecm_rate": 0.6, "ecm_decay": 0.05, "k_bind": 2.0, "spread_rate": 0.5, "max_step": 1.0}, "inputs": {"xs": ["xs"], "ys": ["ys"], "ecm": ["ecm"], "colony": ["colony"]}, "outputs": {"xs": ["xs"], "ys": ["ys"], "ecm": ["ecm"], "colony": ["colony"], "cluster_radius": ["obs", "cluster_radius"], "cohesion": ["obs", "cohesion"], "n_clustered": ["obs", "n_clustered"], "formed": ["obs", "formed"], "ecm_total": ["obs", "ecm_total"]}, "interval_label": "1 s"}, "xs": {"_type": "map", "_value": "float", "0": 12.2, "1": 10.1, "2": 5.9, "3": 3.8, "4": 5.9, "5": 10.1}, "ys": {"_type": "map", "_value": "float", "0": 8.0, "1": 11.6373, "2": 11.6373, "3": 8.0, "4": 4.3627, "5": 4.3627}, "ecm": {"_type": "concentration", "_default": 0.0}, "colony": {"_type": "tree[node]", "cell_0": {"_control": "cell", "contents": {"biomass": 1.0}}, "cell_1": {"_control": "cell", "contents": {"biomass": 1.0}}, "cell_2": {"_control": "cell", "content